(1) **of motion from a place**: [[40-matthew.5.29|Mat.5:29, 30 7:23]], [[42-luke.5.2|Luk.5:2 22:41]], al.; 
(2) in partitive sense (M, _Pr._, 72, 102, 245; MM, see word; Bl., §40, 2), [[40-matthew.9.16|Mat.9:16 27:21]], [[43-john.21.10|Jhn.21:10]], [[44-acts.5.2|Act.5:2]], al.; also after verbs of eating, etc.; 
(3) of alienation (cl. genitive of separation), after such verbs as λούω (Deiss., _BS_, 227), λύω, σώζω, παύω, etc.; ἀνάθεμα ἀ., [[45-romans.9.3|Rom.9:3;]] ἀποθνήσκειν ἀ., [[51-colossians.2.20|Col.2:20;]] σαλευθῆναι, [[53-2-thessalonians.2.2|2Th.2:2]], καθαρός, -ίζειν, ἀ. (Deiss., _BS_, 196, 216), [[44-acts.20.26|Act.20:26]], [[47-2-corinthians.7.1|2Co.7:1]], [[58-hebrews.9.14|Heb.9:14]]; 
(4) of position, [[40-matthew.23.34|Mat.23:34 24:31]], al.; after μακράν, [[40-matthew.8.30|Mat.8:30;]] transposed before measures of distance, [[43-john.10.18|Jhn.10:18 21:8]], [[66-revelation.14.20|Rev.14:20]] (Abbott, _JG_, 227); 
(5) of time, ἀπὸ τ. ὥρας, ἡμέρας, etc., [[40-matthew.9.22|Mat.9:22]], [[43-john.19.27|Jhn.19:27]], [[44-acts.20.18|Act.20:18]], [[50-philippians.1.5|Php.1:5]], al.; ἀπ᾽ αἰῶνος, [[42-luke.1.70|Luk.1:70]], al.; ἀπ᾽ ἀρχῆς, etc., [[40-matthew.19.4|Mat.19:4]], [[45-romans.1.20|Rom.1:20]]; ἀπὸ βρέφους, [[55-2-timothy.3.15|2Ti.3:15;]] ἀφ᾽ ἧς, **since**, [[42-luke.7.45|Luk.7:45]], al.; ἀπὸ τ. νῦν, [[42-luke.1.48|Luk.1:48]], al.; ἀπὸ τότε, [[40-matthew.4.17|Mat.4:17]], al.; ἀπὸ πέρυσι, **a year ago**, [[47-2-corinthians.8.10|2Co.8:10 9:2]]; ἀπὸ πρωΐ, [[44-acts.28.23|Act.28:23;]] 
(6) of order or rank, ἀπὸ διετοῦς, [[40-matthew.2.16|Mat.2:16;]] ἀπὸ Ἀβραάμ, [[40-matthew.1.17|Mat.1:17;]] ἐβδομος ἀπὸ Ἀδάμ, Ju 14; ἀπὸ μικροῦ ἕως μεγάλου, [[44-acts.8.10|Act.8:10]], [[58-hebrews.8.11|Heb.8:11]]; ἄρχεσθαι ἀπό, [[40-matthew.20.8|Mat.20:8]], [[43-john.8.9|Jhn.8:9]], [[44-acts.8.35|Act.8:35]], al. 
2. **Of origin**; 
(1) of birth, extraction, and hence, in late writers, 
(a) of local extraction (cl. ἐξ; Abbott, _JG_, 227ff.), [[40-matthew.21.11|Mat.21:11]], [[41-mark.15.43|Mrk.15:43]], [[43-john.1.45|Jhn.1:45]], [[44-acts.10.38|Act.10:38]], al.; οἱ ἀπὸ Ἰταλίας (WM, §66, 6; M, _Pr._, 237; Westc, Rendall, in l.), [[58-hebrews.13.24|Heb.13:24;]] 
(b) of membership in a community or society (BL, §40, 2), [[44-acts.12.1|Act.12:1]], al.; 
(with) of material (= cl. genitive; Bl. l.with; M, _Pr._, 102), [[40-matthew.3.4|Mat.3:4 27:21]]; 
(d) after verbs of asking, seeking, etc., [[42-luke.11.50|Luk.11:50, 51]] [[52-1-thessalonians.2.6|1Th.2:6]] (Milligan, in l.); 
(2) of the cause, instrument, means or occasion (frequently = ὑπό, παρά, and after verbs of learning, hearing, knowing, etc.; Bl., §40, 3), [[40-matthew.7.16|Mat.7:16 11:29]], [[42-luke.22.45|Luk.22:45]], [[44-acts.2.22|Act.2:22 4:36 9:13 12:14]], [[46-1-corinthians.11.23|1Co.11:23]], [[48-galatians.3.2|Gal.3:2]], al.; ἀπὸ τ. ὄχλου, [[42-luke.19.3|Luk.19:3]] (cf. [[43-john.21.6|Jhn.21:6]], [[44-acts.22.11|Act.22:11]]); ἀπὸ τ. φόβου, [[40-matthew.14.26|Mat.14:26]], al. (cf. [[40-matthew.10.26|Mat.10:26 13:44]]). 
3. **Noteworthy Hellenistic phrases**: φοβεῖσθαι ἀπό (M, _Pr._, 102, 107); προσέχειν ἀπό (M, _Pr._, 11. with; Milligan, _NTD_, 50); ἀπὸ νότου (Heb. מִגֶּנֶב), [[66-revelation.21.13|Rev.21:13;]] ἀπὸ προσώπου (מִפְּנֵי), [[53-2-thessalonians.1.9|2Th.1:9]] (Bl., §40, 9); ἀπὸ τ. καρδιῶν (בְּלֵב), [[40-matthew.18.35|Mat.18:35;]] ἀπὸ ὁ ὤν (WM, §10, 2; M, _Pr._, 9), [[66-revelation.1.4|Rev.1:4.]] 
4. In composition, ἀπό denotes separation, departure, origin, etc. (ἀπολύω, ἀπέρχομαι, ἀπογράφω); it also has a perfective force (M, _Pr._, 112, 247), as in ἀφικνεῖσθαι, which see
(AS)

622:
**ἀπ-όλλυμι and ἀπολλύω **
[in LXX for אָבַד, etc. (38 words in all)]. 
