(b) **with prepositions**: ἐν, of the element, [[40-matthew.3.6|Mat.3:6, 11]] [[41-mark.1.4|Mrk.1:4, 5 8]], [[42-luke.3.16|Luk.3:16]], [[43-john.1.26|Jhn.1:26, 31 33 3:23]], [[44-acts.1.5|Act.1:5 2:38 10:48 11:16]], [[46-1-corinthians.10.2|1Co.10:2]]; εἰς, of the element, purpose or result (Lft., _Notes_, 155), [[40-matthew.3.1|Mat.3:1 28:19]], [[41-mark.1.9|Mrk.1:9]], [[44-acts.8.16|Act.8:16 19:3, 5]] [[45-romans.6.3|Rom.6:3]], 1Co.1:13, 15 10:2 12:13, [[48-galatians.3.27|Gal.3:27]]; with dative, ὕδατι, [[42-luke.3.16|Luk.3:16]], [[44-acts.1.5|Act.1:5 11:16]]; ὑπὲρ τῶν νεκρῶν, perh. to fulfil the wish of a dead friend, [[46-1-corinthians.15.29|1Co.15:29]] (see _ICC_, in l.; cf. _DB_, i, 238ff.; _DCG_, i, 169a; ii, 605b; Cremer, 126).
(AS)

